<%# One application's TEST SUITE across the branch ladder, drawn as a single
    horizontal strip: accepted → release → main, left to right.

    WHAT THE STRIP SAYS. Each badge is one rung's CI verdict, and the three read as a
    progression — the eye follows a suite up the ladder as it is verified at each rung.
    The vocabulary is deliberately the same one tasks/_release_phase_meter and
    components/_ci_progress_meter already teach on this page, so the operator learns it
    once: a TINT fill (15% light / 30% dark) rather than a block of colour, amber while
    work is in flight, emerald when it settles green, rose when it settles bad.

      faded   — NOT VERIFIED. Either nothing was ever built for this rung, or the only
                verdict we hold predates the work now sitting on it. Both mean the same
                thing to an operator deciding whether to trust the rung, so they share
                the faded treatment and differ in their title text.
      amber   — running. CI is processing this rung right now.
      emerald — verified. The suite settled green on what is actually there.
      rose    — failed (or conflicted).

    WHY STALE IS FADED RATHER THAN GREEN. Ci::LadderRung proves staleness from board
    timestamps: a rung is stale when work is parked on it whose merge landed AFTER the
    verdict's run started. A stale green describes a tree that is no longer the tree, so
    painting it green would assert a verification nobody performed. Faded is the honest
    rendering — and it is the same thing the operator needs to know as "never built":
    this rung is not currently verified. Measured 2026-08-19: turf-monster `accepted`
    read green@abe8c51 while its tip was c1959ef, three merges later.

    Locals:
      card       - Ci::AppLadder::Card
      card_class - extra classes for the grid cell %>
<% card = local_assigns.fetch(:card) %>
<% base_card_class = ["rounded-xl border border-subtle bg-surface p-4", local_assigns[:card_class]].compact.join(" ") %>
<% attention = card.needs_attention? %>

<div class="<%= [base_card_class, ("border-amber-500/40" if attention)].compact.join(" ") %>"
     data-test="app-ladder-card"
     data-repo="<%= card.repo %>"
     data-attention="<%= attention %>">
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 mb-2.5 min-w-0">
    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold truncate" title="<%= card.repo %>"><%= card.repo %></h3>
    <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted shrink-0">
      <%= card.gem? ? "gem" : "app" %>
    </span>
  </div>

  <%# The suite strip. role=group with one spelled-out summary carries the whole thing
      to assistive tech; the badges themselves are decorative to it, because reading
      three branch names and three state words in sequence is noise once the summary
      has said it. %>
  <div class="flex items-stretch gap-1"
       data-test="app-ladder-suite"
       role="group"
       aria-label="<%= app_ladder_suite_summary(card) %>">
    <% Ci::AppLadder::RUNGS.each do |branch| %>
      <% rung = card.rung(branch) %>
      <% next if rung.blank? %>
      <% tone = app_ladder_rung_tone(rung.state) %>
      <div class="relative flex-1 min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded border <%= tone[:border] %> bg-inset"
           data-test="app-ladder-rung"
           data-branch="<%= branch %>"
           data-state="<%= rung.state %>"
           title="<%= app_ladder_rung_title(rung) %>">
        <%# The TINT, never a solid block — the label rides on top of it. Same 15/30
            split the release meter measured at 5.3:1 or better in both themes. %>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 <%= tone[:fill] %> opacity-15 dark:opacity-30"
             data-test="app-ladder-rung-fill"></div>
        <div class="relative flex items-center justify-center gap-1 px-1.5 py-1 <%= tone[:text] %>">
          <% if rung.state == :pending %>
            <%# The one moving part: a spinner while the rung is being verified, matching
                the CI meter's running mark. motion-reduce keeps it still for anyone who
                asked for that. %>
            <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0 animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle class="opacity-25" cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/>
              <path class="opacity-90" d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 1 9 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
          <% elsif rung.state == :green %>
            <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="4" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5"/>
            </svg>
          <% elsif %i[red conflicted].include?(rung.state) %>
            <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="4" d="M6 18 18 6M6 6l12 12"/>
            </svg>
          <% end %>
          <span class="truncate text-[10px] font-medium leading-none"><%= branch %></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# Parked work, one quiet line under the strip — how many tasks sit at each rung
      right now. Derived from the board's `merged` column, so it drains on its own as
      a sweep and then a ship advance the stamps. %>
  <% parked = Ci::AppLadder::RUNGS.filter_map { |b| [b, card.rung(b)&.parked_count.to_i] if card.rung(b)&.parked_count.to_i&.positive? } %>
  <% if parked.any? %>
    <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-0.5 text-[10px] text-muted" data-test="app-ladder-parked-row">
      <% parked.each do |branch, count| %>
        <span data-test="app-ladder-parked" data-branch="<%= branch %>">
          <span class="tabular-nums font-medium"><%= count %></span> on <%= branch %>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
